  <running_head>De Bello &amp; Duello.</running_head>
  <page_number>19</page_number>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>quod</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">cum apparatu ludorum,ac sce-</l>
    <l n="2">narum celebratur, quam qui-</l>
    <l n="3">dem in equestri conveniat de-</l>
    <l n="4">curfione. Et otiofis illud ex-</l>
    <l n="5">ercitii genus magis aptum est,</l>
    <l n="6">quam viris in rebus bellicis</l>
    <l n="7">occupatis, quibus ea magis</l>
    <l n="8">placent exercitia, quae non ad</l>
    <l n="9">pompam aut oftentationem</l>
    <l n="10">tantum, sed etiam ad commo-</l>
    <l n="11">ditatem referuntur. Fateor qui-</l>
    <l n="12">dem patrum noftrorum me-</l>
    <l n="13">moriâ ludos hasticos confueto[?]</l>
    <l n="14">more celebratos fuisse, verum</l>
    <l n="15">tum temporis non inutiliter,</l>
    <l n="16">quod cum in praeliis, aut veli-</l>
    <l n="17">tationibus, lanceari pugna-</l>
    <l n="18">rent equites, illius exercitii</l>
    <l n="19">aliquis esset in bello usus;</l>
    <l n="20">quem etiam aliquo cum peri-</l>
    <l n="21">culo redimere, non illicitum</l>
    <l n="22">judicatur. Non aliter atque</l>
    <l n="23">hodierno tempore equitum</l>
    <l n="24">concursus ludicri permissi,</l>
    <l n="25">etiamsi nonnunquam cum ali-</l>
    <l n="26">quo discrimine adhibeantur;</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Long s is printed as plain s throughout. "permiffi" and "fuiffe" are printed with ff for ss and are given as permissi and fuisse. The word "confueto" is printed as shown; the expected form is "consueto", so it is marked [?]. The word "memoriâ" carries a printed mark over the final vowel, copied as given. No margin text, no Greek or Hebrew.</notes>
</page>
